  "body": "## Verdict\n\n**BLOCKED / needs_followup \u2014 repair after Mennonite HOLD.** This draft PR repairs the arithmetic, source, and unsupported-claim defects audited on head `4da753f723c4d8173143016bd224e8b2d39333f4`. It remains an evidence-gap record, is **not ready**, and is **not a request to approve or merge**. A wholly fresh Mennonite must audit the new exact head.\n\n- Old audited head: `4da753f723c4d8173143016bd224e8b2d39333f4`\n- New exact head: `5d5ca1079a406de6c24e688239ec0e9e7cf4deac`\n- Bathcat-Authored: true\n- Audit-Owner: wholly fresh Mennonite\n- Status: `needs_followup`; PR must remain OPEN and DRAFT\n\n## Repair after HOLD\n\nThe repair commit adds the official release-era Wizards rulebook, corrects the governing and component arithmetic, removes two unsupported edge-case statements, cites the live Hasbro detail page for the current FAQ observation, and preserves all verified visual binaries.\n\nRepair-only diff: **9 files, 122 insertions, 46 deletions**. Full PR diff from base: **20 files, 849 insertions, 167 deletions**.\n\n## Official 2018 source receipt\n\nhttps://media.wizards.com/2018/downloads/rules/BLY-Rulebook-web.pdf\n\n- HTTP 200; `application/pdf`; 5,358,358 bytes; 23 pages.\n- SHA-256: `ab30782170e8e8d6c794486385422517aad54e0b2ae2781126bfae30bc11ad5e`.\n- PDF metadata created/modified in 2018.\n- Footer: `TM & \u00a92018 Wizards of the Coast LLC`; code `300C4595000001 EN`.\n- Scope: release-era general rules and starting inventory. It does **not** prove that F3147's haunt books, Bleak Journal, or concealed materials are identical to a particular first printing.\n\n## Governing-rules wording\n\nThe ten rows are a **provisional source-group checklist**, not a closed governing corpus. Four listed source groups have been acquired out of that provisional ten-row checklist. The closed governing denominator and any coverage percentage are **unknown** pending a spoiler-controlled authority inventory.\n\nLegacy parts 1/2 may be one ordered authority split physically; sealed box/envelope are containers until inventoried; and rule-bearing Item/Event/Omen cards, tiles, reference cards, and Monster/Traitor/component text may belong in the denominator because component text can override the rulebook and direct state or victory.\n\nThe 100% gate still fails because at least six listed concealed groups are absent.\n\n## Component arithmetic\n\nStarting inventory is normalized as **22/22 printed inventory lines**. This preserves paired haunt books and paired Legacy decks as printed, keeps `12 tiles` and `20 tile planks` separate, and treats the 122-token total/breakdown as one printed line.\n\nThis is source-level inventory transcription independently recorded by the official 2018 and F3147 rulebooks. Exact-first-print applicability of every physical component and rule-bearing text remains **unverified/unknown**, not zero. No composite factual score is claimed while hidden card/tile identity and readout denominators remain unknown.\n\n## Edge-case and FAQ repairs\n\nRemoved as unsupported edition leakage:\n\n- the statement that prohibition/cannot-happen overrides permission;\n- the statement that unresolved disputes use group decision with the active player breaking ties.\n\nThe remaining conflict hierarchy is limited to what both rulebooks state: haunt text over cards/tiles, and cards/tiles over the rulebook.\n\nThe current Hasbro detail page was rechecked live (SKU F3147, one 10.76 MB download). Its PRODUCT FAQs region displayed generic contact guidance and no product-specific entry. That bounded current-page claim now declares and cites the page source (`src-002`), not the direct PDF.\n\n## Visual disposition\n\nAll four official-rulebook derivatives and the deterministic contact sheet are preserved byte-for-byte; no visual binary or visual metadata was changed by the repair.\n\n## Local gates before commit\n\n- Targeted validation: 13 changed Betrayal Legacy OKF records clean.\n- `node scripts/generate-index.mjs`: completed.\n- Full `node scripts/validate-okf.mjs`: 2,620 files clean; INDEX fresh.\n- Intake/provenance Node tests: 31 pass, 1 skip, 0 fail.\n- `node scripts/validate-intake.mjs --base origin/main`: clean.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- Repository pre-commit and pre-push hooks passed; telemetry committed atomically.\n- GitHub `validate` on exact head `5d5ca1079a406de6c24e688239ec0e9e7cf4deac`: **PASS** (39s) \u2014 https://github.com/no-trbl-2-u/game-knowledge-base/actions/runs/30613914725/job/91102623190.\n\n## Unresolved HOLD conditions / help requested\n\n1. Provide lawful access or an official mapping for a particular English first printing's haunt books, Bleak Journal, and concealed materials; release-era general rules and inventory are already covered by the official 2018 web rulebook.\n2. Authorize a private, spoiler-controlled inventory of both Legacy deck parts, Purgatory, Folium concealed rules, and the actual contents/instructions of the sealed box and envelope.\n3. T/Judge must decide whether every rule-bearing component-local card, tile, and reference card must be atomized or may be represented by a closed source-level ledger.\n\nUntil those conditions are resolved and a wholly fresh Mennonite audits this exact head, this PR remains **HOLD / blocked / needs_followup**, DRAFT, and ineligible for approval or merge.\n",
